        "why": "The only overlap is a short absolute-path check (`Path(path)`, `is_absolute()`, 400 \"Path must be absolute\") and the generic 500 error wrapper. Beyond that, the two endpoints do different things: download checks existence and file type and returns a FileResponse, while upload creates parent directories and streams the body to disk. That check is only a few lines and is not a substantial domain policy. A helper would add little, so I do not treat it as actionable duplication. The error wrapping also differs: download re-raises HTTPException, while upload has no such clause."
